{"profile":{"name":"Jon Burnside","ward":"Ward 16, Don Valley East","bio":"Jon Burnside was elected councillor for Ward 16, Don Valley East, in the 2022 municipal election, returning to City Hall after previously representing Ward 26, Don Valley West, from 2014-2018 (a seat he lost when wards were redrawn). He served as a Toronto Police officer from 1991 to 2001 and later founded and operated a healthy food delivery business in the GTA for about 14 years. He chaired the TTC from November 2022 to August 2023.","committees":["General Government Committee","North York Community Council","Toronto and Region Conservation Authority","Housing Services Corporation"],"contact":{"email":"councillor_burnside@toronto.ca","phone":"416-397-9256"},"promises":[{"text":"Open a local community office in the ward. (Office opened at 895 Lawrence Ave E, Suite 205.)","source":"https://www.dmri.ca/city_council_and_councillor_jon_burnside_update_ward_16_don_valley_east"},{"text":"Hold in-person Open Houses for development applications before the City's virtual consultations. (15 held.)","source":"https://www.dmri.ca/city_council_and_councillor_jon_burnside_update_ward_16_don_valley_east"},{"text":"Add officers to Toronto Police community policing and step up local patrols.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"}]},"lobbying":{"total":693,"term":262,"first":"2014-12-02","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":157,"clients":133,"subjects":301,"methods":{"Meetings":261,"Emails":301,"Phone calls":75,"Written":43,"Other or unreported":13},"top":[{"label":"Economic Development","count":187},{"label":"By-law / Regulation","count":153},{"label":"Licences / Licensing","count":146},{"label":"Planning and Development Application, Zoning By-law","count":108},{"label":"Signs","count":75}],"years":[{"year":2014,"count":7},{"year":2015,"count":115},{"year":2016,"count":142},{"year":2017,"count":118},{"year":2018,"count":49},{"year":2022,"count":20},{"year":2023,"count":99},{"year":20